Cc: nethack-bugs@linc.cis.upenn.edu

Many people have complained that the install program in ChrHack kills the
config file when run.  Well, I started looking for the bug.

I kept trying test cases on my IBM at home, and the Install program kept
working perfecly.  So I got upset, downloaded both nethack and chrhack20 from
wuarhcive, unzip/unarjed 'em both, and ran install.  

It choked!

But I found out why:

The Nethack.cnf file included in the PC distribution is in UNIX format.  (ie,
^J at the end of lines instead of ^M), hence install was reading the file as
one line, and because the string type only has 255 chars, then the line was
getting truncated at 255.

If the file is converted to ibm format (using flip for example, available in
wuarchive.wustl.edu:/mirrors/msdos/txtutl/flip1exe.arc) then the install
program functions perfectly.

I'm sending this to the nethack bugs in the hope that they will fix the
official PC archive to have a DOS style config file, not a UNIX style one.

